Description: Extend the generic AT-probe window (18 s -> 42 s) for slow modems.
 ModemManager 1.20.6 sends the generic "AT" port probe up to 6 times with a
 3-second timeout each (src/mm-port-probe.c: at_probing[]), giving a serial
 port only ~18 s to answer before it is classified as non-AT.  When no AT port
 answers, MM logs "Failed to find primary AT port" and creates no modem
 object.  Some Telit modems (notably FN920C04, firmware M0V.060001) can take
 longer than 18 s to bring their AT command stack up after USB enumeration, so
 MM gives up too early and the device shows "no modem" until something forces a
 re-probe (e.g. a ModemManager restart).
 .
 Upstream ModemManager (>= 1.24) solves this with the per-port
 ID_MM_TTY_AT_PROBE_TRIES udev tag (default 6, max 20; each try is 3 s) -- see
 include/ModemManager-tags.h -- but that tag mechanism does not exist in
 1.20.6.  As the 1.20.6-era equivalent, grow the shared at_probing[] array from
 6 to 14 entries so a slow port gets up to 42 s (14 x 3 s) to respond -- the
 same probe budget upstream applies to the FN920C04.
 .
 A port that answers responds on the first probe and returns immediately, so
 healthy modems are unaffected; only a genuinely slow or unresponsive AT port
 consumes the longer window.  With the port-type rules in
 0002-telit-fn920c04-fn990b40-port-types.patch the AT probe is confined to the
 AT-primary port on the FN920C04, so the extra time is not spent blind-probing
 its GPS/QCDM ports.  Because 1.20.6 has no per-PID probe count, this window
 applies to every AT probe; to change it, add or remove "AT" lines in the array
 (max 20 = 60 s, matching the upstream ID_MM_TTY_AT_PROBE_TRIES ceiling).
 .
 NOTE: this only helps the slow-to-become-ready case.  It does NOT recover a
 hard command-stack wedge (a port dead for minutes) -- that still requires a
 modem reset.
Author: VyOS / iGOS WWAN team
Last-Update: 2026-08-21
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: backport-equivalent of ID_MM_TTY_AT_PROBE_TRIES=14 (ModemManager >= 1.24)

--- a/src/mm-port-probe.c
+++ b/src/mm-port-probe.c
@@ -1104,6 +1104,14 @@
     { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
     { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
     { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
+    { "AT",  3, mm_port_probe_response_processor_is_at },
     { NULL }
 };
 
